Package: karst
Title: KARST: Karyotype Abundance-Based Reconstruction of Fitness Landscape from Sparse Time Points
Version: 1.1.3
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Richard", family = "Beck",
           email = "richard.beck@moffitt.org", role = "aut"),
    person(given = "Tao", family = "Li",
           email = "Tao.Li2@moffitt.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Author: Richard Beck [aut], Tao Li [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Tao Li <Tao.Li2@moffitt.org>
Description: KARST (Karyotype Abundance-based Reconstruction of fitness
    landscape from Sparse Time points) infers fitness landscapes of aneuploid
    karyotypes from sparse single-cell karyotype counts at two or more time
    points. Its default model, the sparse joint count model, fits the counts
    of the well-sampled karyotypes and of all their one-step neighbours,
    observed or not, with one likelihood, and predicts fitness further away
    from a fitted trend. It writes the outputs of alfak (the R package alfakR
    of the ALFA-K paper), so that analyses built on alfak read its results
    unchanged. KARST was released as alfak2 up to version 0.2.0.
URL: https://github.com/TaoLee0510/karst
